---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { getData } from "../../lib/data";
import { TABLES } from "../../lib/export";
const d = getData();
const counts = { events: d.events.length, people: d.people.length, organizations: d.organizations.length, sources: d.sources.length };
---
<Base title="Download the data" description="Every case, person, organization, status entry, dollar figure, and source as CSV and JSON, licensed CC BY 4.0.">
  <h1>Download the data</h1>
  <p class="summary">All of the data behind this site is free to download and reuse under the <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0</a> license. Please credit "Federal Fraud and Public Corruption Tracker". Government and court documents are in the public domain. The files are rebuilt every time the site is updated.</p>
  <p>The current files cover {counts.events} cases, {counts.people} people, {counts.organizations} organizations, and {counts.sources} sources.</p>

  <h2>Complete dataset</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/downloads/dataset.json" download>dataset.json</a>: every record exactly as stored, plus a <code>derived</code> block for each case with its computed case status, resolution date, and each participant's current status.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tables (CSV)</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <caption>CSV files. Lists inside a cell are separated by semicolons. Dates may be a year, a month, or a full date, as precise as the source.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">File</th><th scope="col">Contents</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {Object.entries(TABLES).map(([file, t]) => (
          <tr><td><a href={`/downloads/${file}`} download>{file}</a></td><td>{t.description}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Reading the data correctly</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Status belongs to each person or organization, not to the case. A case is "resolved" only when everyone in it is.</li>
    <li>Every dollar figure has a basis: <strong>alleged</strong> (from a charging document), <strong>admitted</strong>, <strong>adjudicated</strong>, or <strong>estimated</strong>. Do not add alleged amounts to totals, and do not add different measures together.</li>
    <li>Inclusion is not a finding of guilt. See <a href="/about/">status definitions and the disclaimer</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
